From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: uvcvideo: Don't report resubmitting a poisoned URB as
 an error

uvc_video_stop_transfer() poisons the video URBs, rather than killing
them, so that the asynchronous copy work cannot resubmit them after the
completion handler has returned. A URB that completed just before it
was poisoned is still handed to uvc_video_complete() or to the copy
work, whose usb_submit_urb() then fails with -EPERM, exactly as
intended. Both places log that as

  uvcvideo 7-1.4:1.1: Failed to resubmit video URB (-1).

so every stream stop can print an error although nothing went wrong.
On an RK3588 board capturing short clips from a UVC webcam it shows up
on the console every few minutes.

-EPERM from usb_submit_urb() only means the URB was poisoned or is being
killed, which the driver only does when stopping the stream: don't log
it. Other failures are still reported.

Link: https://bugzilla.kernel.org/show_bug.cgi?id=217924
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
--- a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
@@ -1351,8 +1351,12 @@
 		uvc_queue_buffer_release(op->buf);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * -EPERM means the URB has been poisoned by uvc_video_stop_transfer(),
+	 * which is how stopping the stream keeps this work from resubmitting.
+	 */
 	ret = usb_submit_urb(uvc_urb->urb, GFP_KERNEL);
-	if (ret < 0)
+	if (ret < 0 && ret != -EPERM)
 		dev_err(&uvc_urb->stream->intf->dev,
 			"Failed to resubmit video URB (%d).\n", ret);
 }
@@ -1781,7 +1785,8 @@
 	/* If no async work is needed, resubmit the URB immediately. */
 	if (!uvc_urb->async_operations) {
 		ret = usb_submit_urb(uvc_urb->urb, GFP_ATOMIC);
-		if (ret < 0)
+		/* -EPERM: poisoned by uvc_video_stop_transfer(), see above. */
+		if (ret < 0 && ret != -EPERM)
 			dev_err(&stream->intf->dev,
 				"Failed to resubmit video URB (%d).\n", ret);
 		return;
-- 
2.51.0
